{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `W_z1`, `Y_z1_w1`, `Y_z1_w0`, `Y_z0_w0`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target +=` likelihood with built-in, vectorized Bernoulli sampling statements over deterministic top-level reshapes of the observed data. The generated data fields are defined as `W_z1 = W[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1`; `Y_z1_w1 = Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1 && W[n] == 1`; `Y_z1_w0 = Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 1 && W[n] == 0`; and `Y_z0_w0 = Y[n]` for rows with `Z[n] == 0 && W[n] == 0`, with matching `N_*` lengths. Rows with `Z[n] == 0 && W[n] == 1` are not copied because the original program added no likelihood term for them. The `log_mix` Bernoulli mixture for `Z == 0, W == 0` was rewritten exactly as a Bernoulli likelihood with probability `pi_c * eta_c0 + (1 - pi_c) * eta_n0`. Added the explicit density-neutral prior `pi_c ~ uniform(0, 1)` for the bounded parameter that previously had an implicit uniform prior.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N_z1;
  array[N_z1] int<lower=0, upper=1> W_z1;

  int<lower=0> N_z1_w1;
  array[N_z1_w1] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z1_w1;

  int<lower=0> N_z1_w0;
  array[N_z1_w0] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z1_w0;

  int<lower=0> N_z0_w0;
  array[N_z0_w0] int<lower=0, upper=1> Y_z0_w0;
}

parameters {
  // Population probability of being a complier
  real<lower=0, upper=1> pi_c;

  // Probabilities for the binomial outcome distributions
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_c0;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_c1;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_n0;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> eta_n1;
} 

model {
  // Prior for Complier probability
  pi_c ~ uniform(0, 1);

  // Priors for outcome model parameters
  eta_c0 ~ beta(2, 2);  
  eta_c1 ~ beta(2, 2);  
  eta_n0 ~ beta(2, 2);
  eta_n1 ~ beta(2, 2);

  // Likelihood
  W_z1 ~ bernoulli(pi_c);
  Y_z1_w1 ~ bernoulli(eta_c1);
  Y_z1_w0 ~ bernoulli(eta_n1);
  Y_z0_w0 ~ bernoulli(pi_c * eta_c0 + (1 - pi_c) * eta_n0);
}

generated quantities {
  // Super-population average causal effects 
  real CACE = (eta_c1 - eta_c0) * 10^3;
  real NACE = (eta_n1 - eta_n0) * 10^3;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N_z1":1,"W_z1":[1],"N_z1_w1":1,"Y_z1_w1":[0],"N_z1_w0":0,"Y_z1_w0":[],"N_z0_w0":0,"Y_z0_w0":[]}","protected_variables":["W_z1","Y_z1_w1","Y_z1_w0","Y_z0_w0"]}
